Polarization is a threshold phenomenon (1.3.32) in organizational
dress; report-card language (mean square error beside F1-style scores) is at 1.3.38.
# Paper 005 — DELTA: Braided multisections and Akhmedov's fake quadrics
arXiv:2611.06949 [math.GT], v1, submitted 3 Nov 2026. CC0.
Anar Akhmedov (University of Minnesota). Pure mathematics: symplectic
and geometric topology of 4-manifolds. Builds on the cyclic of the author
construction with Baldridge, integral Mayer-Vietoris formulas with
Yeung, and an earlier knot-surgery construction (paper refs [5][6][8]).

DELTA STATEMENT — relative to the model at Paper 004: total domain
break. Nothing in this paper uses again, changes, or contradicts any
canonical scroll from Papers 001-004; it adds as a new wing a new field
(cluster E, concept map 1.1.5). New canonical concepts: 1.2.34-1.2.39.
Canonical scrolls revised: NONE — recorded explicitly, because in this
model 'no revision' across a domain break is information, not an
omission. What the paper adds internally: explicit handlebody
recipes in parts of the multisection complements M_{2,3}, M_{3,2},
M_{2,4}; integral homology of complements including H_2 torsion and
its geometric generator; marked surface diffeomorphisms realizing the
Akhmedov-Yeung gluing matrices for the (3,3) and (2,4) families; the
resulting sums shown aspherical and symplectically minimal.
# Paper 005 — DELTA: results (all statements as reported in the paper;
Theorem 1.1, Theorem 2.3, Prop 5.1 and Cors 2.4/5.2/5.3 cross-checked
between introduction, section statements and appendix by Emise,
2026-11-06 — proofs not independently verified; mathematics is
reported at theorem level, as with prior papers' experiments)

MAIN THEOREM (Theorem 1.1): the complements M_{2,3}, M_{3,2}, M_{2,4} admit
the handlebody recipes in parts of §2 with handle counts (2,11,14,3),
(2,14,14,2), (2,12,18,4) respectively. For each m >= 1, the symplectic
sums Z_m^{3,3} and Z_m^{2,4} formed with the marked diffeomorphisms
f_m of §§3-4 (gluing phi_m(w, e^{i theta}) = (f_m(w), e^{-i theta}),
no surface-dependent normal twist) satisfy:
  H_1(Z_m^{3,3}) ~= (Z/3)^2 ⊕ Z/(3m);  H_1(Z_m^{2,4}) ~= (Z/2)^2 ⊕ Z/(4m);
Euler characteristic 4, signature 0, rational cohomology ring of
S^2 x S^2; both families aspherical and symplectically minimal.
COMPLEMENT HOMOLOGY (Theorem 2.3, Cor 2.4): H_2(M_{g,p}; Z) ~=
Z^{1+2(g-1)(p-1)} ⊕ Z/p, torsion generated by [S_S] - [S_N], the
difference of the pole sections (independent check in App. C).
Being aspherical (Prop 5.1): holds for ANY boundary gluing of two such
complements, via amalgamated pi_1 over the boundary group and a
Bass-Serre tree of contractible pieces; being minimal follows (Cor 5.2).
FULL SUM HOMOLOGY (Cor 5.3): H_2(Z) ~= Z^2 ⊕ T with T = H_1(Z);
H_3 = 0 by integral Poincare duality since T is finite.
SYMMETRIC CASE EXTRA (Theorem B.1): for the m = 1 (3,3) sum, a simultaneous
surface diagram of the relative product attachments, identifying
product framings with surface framings.
CONTEXT FROM INTRODUCTION: the same complements with a sphere fiber
also removed give Stein filling spaces including infinitely many two by two
not the same shape aspherical filling spaces of ONE contact 3-manifold with
identical integral homology (paper ref [7]) — distinguished only by
H_1 of finite covers. Announced follow-up [9] (with Akbulut, Yildiz):
full handlebody diagrams of the closed sums.
# Paper 005 — DELTA: tensions, limits, scope
What this paper does NOT do (scope, from its own framing): it works
two of the three classified degree pairs — (2,3) sums are not given
marked gluings here; the closed sums' complete handle diagrams are
put off to the announced follow-up; no complex or algebraic structure
on the fake quadrics is claimed or needed; aspherical + minimal +
rationally-standard does not classify — the families are distinguished
by |H_1| orders, and whether distinct m or cross-family pairs could
still be diffeomorphic through some invariant not computed here is a
classification question the paper does not close (see Q15).
Verification posture (Emise): theorem statements were cross-checked
for internal consistency across abstract/introduction/sections/
appendices; the handle-diagram and chain-complex computations
themselves were NOT re-derived. This matches the posture of the tracker on
experimental papers (reported, cross-checked, not replicated) — with
the difference that a proof, unlike an experiment, is that can be checked in
principle line by line, and this ingestion did not do that.
# [synthesis] Paper 005 x the model so far — Emise's links, not the claims of the paper
Filed 2026-11-06. Labelled synthesis per charter rule 3. These links
are META-LEVEL analogies, flagged as such; cluster E makes no contact
with clusters A-D at the level of content.

1. Invariant granularity. The fake quadrics pass every RATIONAL test
   for being S^2 x S^2 and fail the INTEGRAL ones; their identity
   lives in torsion, the part the move to fractions deletes. The AI papers
   keep teaching the same lesson at their own level: Paper 001 —
   benchmark scores (coarse) vs sorting/scale structure (fine);
   Paper 003 — style features (coarse, that can be erased) vs discourse
   structure (fine, durable); Paper 002 — task pass/fail (coarse) vs
   cost-annotated history (fine). Candidate invariant of this
   world-model, now with a mathematical witness: when two things look
   identical, the difference is in the invariant you haven't computed
   yet — and the deleted part of your measurement is where to look.
2. Data vs summary. 'The matrices alone do not determine the smooth
   sums' (Paper 005, §1) is the topological form of a recurring claim
   here: Paper 002's contracts exist because the SUMMARY of a policy (its
   interface) doesn't determine its behavior; Paper 004's gate needs
   hidden representations, not input summaries. Presentation is not
   the object; gluing data is not its matrix.
3. About the stream itself [synthesis]: Will's sampling jumped from
   FPGA machine learning to symplectic topology in one step. The
   tracker now holds two continents joined by method-level analogy
   only. That is the honest state, and the Oracle ledger prices it.
